    "explanation": "The provided evidence from pmid-27032107 describes a prospective phase II study evaluating first-line erlotinib in patients with advanced lung adenocarcinoma carrying a somatic EGFR mutation. The study explicitly lists p.Leu858Arg (L858R) as one of the mutations found (15 cases) and concludes that erlotinib was 'highly effective in the majority of the patients' with these somatic EGFR mutations. This directly supports the claim that Erlotinib is effective (sensitivity/response) for Lung Adenocarcinoma with somatic EGFR L858R mutation.",
